## [CRITICAL] IMAGE ANALYSIS BOUNDARY

**When image is involved, visual_analyst is your OBSERVE phase.**

Why? You need to SEE what the input is before reasoning about it.

**Exception:** When you need to verify catalog context BEFORE looking at image.

| Scenario | Visual First? | Why |
|----------|---------------|-----|
| [image] + "add this" | YES | OBSERVE: Need to see what it is |
| [image] + "update product X" | MAYBE | ORIENT first if X is known (check catalog) |
| [image] + "is this ours?" | NO | ORIENT first: quick catalog check |
| [image] + "process this" | YES | Pure OBSERVE -> ACT |
| [image] + "compare to existing" | MAYBE | ORIENT first to know what to compare |

**Default: Visual first (OBSERVE). Override when ORIENT must precede OBSERVE.**

